          "UNRESOLVED (p.69, p.70): CONFLICT (p.69 table vs p.69 / p.70 member lengths): working point L13 - the ELEVATIONS table prints 140.7820 for the CL of lower chord at 13 while the member lengths L12-L13, L13-L14, U12-L13 and U13-L14 all close on 140.7620 (the wind chord value of that row). L13 / L13\u0027 modeled at El. 140.7620 (the lengths govern; the 0.02 ft difference is reported by check-truss-ptc.csx).",
          "UNRESOLVED (p.85, p.94): floor beam end connections - the framed (p.85) and suspended (p.94) end details were not read in full. framed floor beams (points 0-13) end 1\u0027-2 1/2 from the truss CL (the members\u0027 outer face line), suspended ones at the truss CL.",
          "UNRESOLVED (p.71): floor lateral pattern W14-W22 - the diagram summary gives X bracing \u0027in pairs of panels\u0027 W14-W21 and 2-12[ 25 members W21-W22-W21\u0027 without the crossing / connection details. X in W14-16, 16-18, 18-20, 20-21 (14 BP 73) and W21-22 (2-12[ 25).",
          "UNRESOLVED (p.71): lower lateral double K L13-L13 1/2 and the 33 WF 130 strut at L13 1/2; the inverted portal L13 1/2-L15 (Sheets 44 / 45) - the L13 1/2 point is not dimensioned on the sheets read. not built.",
          "UNRESOLVED (p.71): sway bracing above the floor beams and the portal knee bracing - only the V frames below the floor beams are tabulated on p.71. V frames 0-12 built; nothing above the floor beams except the U11 portal strut envelope.",
          "UNRESOLVED (p.94, p.86): upper pin of the rope suspenders - p.94 details the socket and the floor beam end only; the suspender support diaphragm at the lower chord is on Sheet 46 (p.86, not read). upper pin 2\u0027-11 1/4 below the CL of the lower chord (half chord depth 1\u0027-5 1/4 \u002B 1\u0027-6 as at the floor beam).",
